--------------------------------------------------------------------

Features
-User registration with server-side validation
-Passwords hashed with argon2
-TOTP 2FA (Compatible with Google Authenticator)
-Account lockout after repeated failed login attempts
-CSRF protection on every forum
-Session cookies configured
-Append only audit log of login activity

--------------------------------------------------------------------

Setup
-pip install -r requirements.txt
-python app.py

--------------------------------------------------------------------

Function
-Register (/register) creates an account with hashed password
-Setup 2FA (/setup-2fa) scan QR code or manually input into authenticater app
-Log in (/login) enter username and password
-Verify 2FA (/login/verify) enter current verification code from authenticator app
-Dashboard (/dashboard) reached only after login and 2fa verified

--------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose (Threat prevention)
-Database breach: passwords only stored as argon2 hashes, so stolen database doesn't hand over usable credentials.
-Brute-force: accounts lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed login attemps.
-Username enumeration: login errors are identical whether the username doesn't exist or the password is wrong.
-Stolen or guessed passwords: 2fa is required for every login attempt before account is usable.
-CSRF: every form requires a valid CSRF token.
-Cookies: cookies are HTTP only, so client-side javascript can't read them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------

Future Plans
-real HTTPS: run behidn a reverse proxy with a TLS certificate
-IP rate limiting: current lockout is per account only; one person could still hammer many different accounts from one IP